All modern browsers support theXMLHttpRequestobject.

TheXMLHttpRequestobject can be used to exchange data with a web server behind the 
scenes. This means that it is possible to update parts of a web page, without 
reloading the whole page.

All modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, IE, Edge, Safari, Opera) have a built-inXMLHttpRequestobject.

